# ── X-Plane Virtual ATC — local config ──────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env`, or just set these in the app's Settings view.
#
# The defaults need two things:
#   1. A Claude subscription — the controller's brain. Nothing goes here; the
#      app uses the `claude` CLI you sign into separately.
#   2. An ElevenLabs API key (below) — the default provider for BOTH the
#      controller's voice (text-to-speech) and understanding you (speech-to-text).

# Required for speech in/out. Create a key at:
#   https://elevenlabs.io/app/developers/api-keys
# Give the key these permissions (or leave it unrestricted):
#   • Text to Speech  — access   (the controller's voice)
#   • Speech to Text  — access   (transcribes what you say)
#   • User            — read     (lets the app verify the key on startup)
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Controller voice. Use a name from the curated list below, or paste any raw
# voice id from your ElevenLabs library. These are premade ElevenLabs voices
# that read well as a controller — steady, clear, broadcaster/news delivery.
#   daniel   British · deep · news presenter   (default)
#   brian    American · deep · calm narration
#   george   British · warm
#   bill     American · older · documentary
#   adam     American · deep · neutral
#   liam     American · articulate
#   charlie  Australian · conversational
#   alice    British · female · confident news
#   matilda  American · female · warm
#   lily     British · female · warm
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=daniel

# X-Plane install path — only needed if it's NOT in the default Steam location.
# Used to find apt.dat (airport data). The Settings view can set this too.
# XPLANE_PATH=/Applications/X-Plane 12

# Push-to-talk: bind your key to the "xPilot: Radio Push-to-Talk" command and
# leave this as-is. Empty = use the on-screen button / spacebar instead.
XPLANE_PTT_DATAREF=xpilot/ptt

# Auto-set a "VFR day" once at startup, as soon as X-Plane is connected and a
# flight is loaded: real weather frozen (wind/pressure/temp stay real), a few
# scattered clouds, visibility > 5 sm, local noon. Same as the VFR Day button.
# VFR_WEATHER_ON_START=true

# Optional — alternative voice provider (used only if no ElevenLabs key):
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Background traffic (the "party line") ────────────────────────────────────
# Other aircraft on your frequency, injected into the audio while X-Plane is
# connected. Matched to the station you're tuned to and the airport's size; it
# goes quiet the moment you key the mic. Density: off | light | medium | heavy.
# AMBIENT_TRAFFIC_LEVEL=medium
# Flight rules the traffic flies. VFR-only by default; "VFR,IFR" mixes airliners
# in at a field. En-route is always VFR regardless.
# AMBIENT_TRAFFIC_RULES=VFR
# The OTHER pilots each get a voice from a pool, picked by their callsign so one
# aircraft stays consistent. By default the pool matches your TTS backend — with
# ElevenLabs that's 10 distinct voices, chosen to never sound like the controller.
# Override with a comma-separated list: ElevenLabs ids or names from the list
# above, or OpenAI/say voice names. Empty = the backend default pool.
# AMBIENT_PILOT_VOICES=
# Optional directory of your own interaction *.json files, merged on top of the
# built-in library at traffic/interactions/. This is how you customise the chatter.
# AMBIENT_LIBRARY_DIR=
